-1.0371154530730564e-05,-4.887569048150908e-06,-2.50339189733495e-06,-5.960446742392378e-06,-6.9141146923357155e-06,0.0,-3.576278118089249e-07,-0.48448115587234497,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,-2.6940935640595853e-05,0.0,0.0,0.0,-3.576278118089249e-07,0.0,0.0,0.0,-0.4818924367427826,-0.33946728706359863,-0.01135824155062437,0.0,0.0,-7.271740287251305e-06,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,-0.0002420847595203668,-4.291525328881107e-06,-2.3841830625315197e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,10061,400,69,62,16,54876,400,69,62,17,54876,400,69,62,18,54876,57960,67816,3,387,264,8500,315,5109,1741,429,198,59,9640,220,282,1089,284,282,15159,77,481,220,16,92,488,282,15159,77,481,220,17,532,59,60,1958,1449,7546,400,77,1124,709,220,18,12947,220,1416,400,69,62,22,284,220,23,18,54876,1128,374,279,2629,315,279,1156,220,16,15,3793,315,279,8500,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nLet $f_1$, $f_2$, $f_3$, $\\dots$ be a sequence of numbers such that\n\\[\n  f_n = f_{n - 1} + f_{n - 2}\n\\]for every integer $n \\ge 3$.  If $f_7 = 83$, what is the sum of the first 10 terms of the sequence?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"15f9e6e33af29f08f5272d6d917c8a75e8f65becc78e49e0c1c1b49019488b42"},"seconds":80.48064613342285,"seed":780468505852920839,"stop":"eos","text":"Given the recurrence relation \\( f_n = f_{n-1} + f_{n-2} \\) for \\( n \\ge 3 \\) and the value \\( f_7 = 83 \\), we need to find the sum of the first 10 terms of the sequence \\( f_1, f_2, f_3, \\ldots, f_{10} \\).\n\nFirst, let's express the terms \\( f_3 \\) through \\( f_7 \\) in terms of \\( f_1 \\) and \\( f_2 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nf_3 &= f_2 + f_1, \\\\\nf_4 &= f_3 + f_2 = (f_2 + f_1) + f_2 = f_1 + 2f_2, \\\\\nf_5 &= f_4 + f_3 = (f_1 + 2f_2) + (f_2 + f_1) = 2f_1 + 3f_2, \\\\\nf_6 &= f_5 + f_4 = (2f_1 + 3f_2) + (f_1 + 2f_2) = 3f_1 + 5f_2, \\\\\nf_7 &= f_6 + f_5 = (3f_1 + 5f_2) + (2f_1 + 3f_2) = 5f_1 + 8f_2.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nWe know that \\( f_7 = 83 \\), so we have:\n\n\\[\n5f_1 + 8f_2 = 83.\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to find \\( f_8 \\) through \\( f_{10} \\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nf_8 &= f_7 + f_6 = 83 + (3f_1 + 5f_2) = 83 + 3f_1 + 5f_2, \\\\\nf_9 &= f_8 + f_7 = (83 + 3f_1 + 5f_2) + 83 = 166 + 3f_1 + 5f_2, \\\\\nf_{10} &= f_9 + f_8 = (166 + 3f_1 + 5f_2) + (83 + 3f_1 + 5f_2) = 249 + 6f_1 + 10f_2.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to find the sum of the first 10 terms:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\nS &= f_1 + f_2 + f_3 + f_4 + f_5 + f_6 + f_7 + f_8 + f_9 + f_{10} \\\\\n  &= f_1 + f_2 + (f_2 + f_1) + (f_1 + 2f_2) + (2f_1 + 3f_2) + (3f_1 + 5f_2) + 83 + (83 + 3f_1 + 5f_2) + (166 + 3f_1 + 5f_2) + (249 + 6f_1 + 10f_2) \\\\\n  &= f_1 + f_2 + f_2 + f_1 + f_1 + 2f_2 + 2f_1 + 3f_2 + 3f_1 + 5f_2 + 83 + 83 + 3f_1 + 5f_2 + 166 + 3f_1 + 5f_2 + 249 + 6f_1 + 10f_2 \\\\\n  &= (1 + 1 + 1 + 2 + 3 + 3 + 3 + 6)f_1 + (1 + 2 + 3 + 5 + 5 + 5 + 10)f_2 + (83 + 83 + 166 + 249) \\\\\n  &= 20f_1 + 31f_2 + 581.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nFrom the equation \\( 5f_1 + 8f_2 = 83 \\), we need to find integer solutions for \\( f_1 \\) and \\( f_2 \\). We can solve for \\( f_1 \\) and \\( f_2 \\):\n\n\\[\n\\begin{align*}\n5f_1 + 8f_2 &= 83, \\\\\n5(17 - 8k) + 8(5k - 7) &= 83, \\\\\n85 - 40k + 40k - 56 &= 83, \\\\\n29 &= 83.\n\\end{align*}\n\\]\n\nTesting specific values, we find \\( f_1 = 17 \\) and \\( f_2 = 5 \\):\n\n\\[\n5(17) + 8(5) = 85 + 40 = 83.\n\\]\n\nThus, substituting \\( f_1 = 17 \\) and \\( f_2 = 5 \\) into the sum formula:\n\n\\[\nS = 20(17) + 31(5) + 581 = 340 + 155 + 581 = 1076.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the sum of the first 10 terms is \\(\\boxed{1076}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{1076}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
